{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbKd5SFQVya2Lvufzt7w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, and the admission self-check passed (`OK`). It refines the incumbent, `mirror_symmetry_streak_aversion_lapse`, under the name `personal_decisiveness_mirror_streak_lapse`.\n\n**The change:** each person now has their own overall decisiveness, a single number that multiplies the whole score difference between the two sequences before the choice is made. Across people it follows a log-normal distribution with median 1 (`sigma_decisive` ~ HalfNormal(0.5), non-centred, 400 slots). Some people therefore follow their impression of which sequence looks random sharply, and others only weakly, without actually guessing. Everything else in the incumbent is unchanged: the personal ideal alternation rate, the personal weights on heads/tails imbalance and on the longest streak, the shared weights on the final streak and on palindromes, and the personal lapse rate.\n\n**Why this change:** the critique's one flagged discrepancy is that people differ more than the incumbent predicts in how often they agree with the majority choice (observed spread 0.177 against 0.162 predicted). It is only a screening result, though: p = 0.028, and it doesn't survive the false-discovery correction (q = 0.21). The incumbent's personal weights and lapse rates don't fully produce that spread, and a personal decisiveness addresses it directly.\n\n**What the check showed:** the code passed the import rules, the module-level model, a finite log-probability and the data contract. The short smoke fit (one chain, 100 draws) gave a finite ELPD-LOO of −2303.8. Two caveats:\n- **Reliability:** PSIS-LOO came out unreliable on that smoke fit, with 8% of trials having a high Pareto k against a 1% tolerance. A 100-draw fit may well cause this, but if it persists in admission's full fit, the model's ELPD will be marked untrustworthy.\n- **Not tested:** the check doesn't cover convergence, novelty or the 30-minute time limit. Convergence is the main risk: the per-person decisiveness may trade off against the per-person balance and streak weights. The smoke fit took 58 seconds.\n\nThe three files are in `.../experiment2/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_3/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2315,"cache_read_input_tokens":70737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2315,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c59e7e96-0aa2-46b1-9eed-fd21aa789405","uuid":"c65e6e30-58f0-465c-bd43-7d614b5ee592","timestamp":"2026-10-01T10:00:03.797Z","request_id":"req_011CfbKd4yDves7eHjrXSG1W"}
